WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.409
MAID by province.

00:00:01.409 --> 00:00:04.454
Per-capita death rates across all ten provinces.

00:00:04.454 --> 00:00:08.386
Which regions of Canada administer the most state-facilitated deaths?

00:00:08.386 --> 00:00:11.147
All data from Health Canada's annual reports.

00:00:11.147 --> 00:00:14.625
Quebec leads at sixty-three point two per hundred thousand.

00:00:14.625 --> 00:00:17.579
British Columbia follows at fifty-one point eight.

00:00:17.579 --> 00:00:20.829
P.E.I. has the lowest rate at thirteen point nine.

00:00:20.829 --> 00:00:22.897
Twenty twenty-four per-capita rates.

00:00:22.897 --> 00:00:26.443
Quebec: sixty-three point two per hundred thousand.

00:00:26.443 --> 00:00:29.124
British Columbia: fifty-one point eight.

00:00:29.124 --> 00:00:31.715
Ontario: thirty-nine point one.

00:00:31.715 --> 00:00:34.103
Manitoba: thirty-four point seven.

00:00:34.103 --> 00:00:36.613
Alberta: thirty-one point six.

00:00:36.613 --> 00:00:39.113
Nova Scotia: thirty point three.

00:00:39.113 --> 00:00:41.704
New Brunswick: twenty-six point five.

00:00:41.704 --> 00:00:43.806
Saskatchewan: twenty-four.

00:00:43.806 --> 00:00:46.477
Newfoundland: eighteen point nine.

00:00:46.477 --> 00:00:49.465
Prince Edward Island: thirteen point nine.

00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:51.306
What the provincial data reveals.

00:00:51.306 --> 00:00:57.761
Quebec's rate is double the national average — it was the first province to legalize assisted dying in twenty fourteen.

00:00:57.761 --> 00:01:02.568
British Columbia is second highest and climbing faster than any other province.

00:01:02.568 --> 00:01:05.715
The prairie provinces are below average but rising.

00:01:05.715 --> 00:01:15.318
Atlantic Canada has the lowest rates despite having Canada's oldest populations, suggesting MAID uptake is driven by institutional infrastructure rather than demographic need.

00:01:15.318 --> 00:01:21.522
P.E.I.'s rate is less than one quarter of Quebec's — a four point five times difference under the same federal law.

00:01:21.522 --> 00:01:22.921
Year-over-year growth.

00:01:22.921 --> 00:01:31.818
Quebec: from sixteen thirty-two deaths in twenty nineteen to five thousand four hundred and thirty-one in twenty twenty-four — plus two hundred and thirty-three percent.

00:01:31.818 --> 00:01:35.102
Ontario: plus two hundred and twenty-eight percent.

00:01:35.102 --> 00:01:38.818
British Columbia: plus one hundred and ninety-seven percent.

00:01:38.818 --> 00:01:42.522
Alberta: plus one hundred and seventy-six percent.

00:01:42.522 --> 00:01:51.965
Canada total: from five thousand six hundred and thirty-one to sixteen thousand four hundred and ninety-nine — plus one hundred and ninety-three percent growth in five years.

